Chapter 1
Return, and the risks a company carries
العائد والمخاطر التي تتحملها الشركة
Book 1 ended with a verdict on Orontes: strong, well funded, and giving away two points of gross margin to buy growth. Every figure in it was historical. This book is about the other direction in time — the money a company raises, the price it pays for it, and the decisions it takes with it — and every one of those is a decision under uncertainty.
Uncertainty is the subject of this chapter. A shareholder who earned 19.30 per cent on Orontes in 2025 did not know in January what the year would bring, and neither did the bank that lent at 6 per cent. What each of them did know was the shape of what could happen, and that shape has a name, a measure, and a price. Everything in Section B rests on the two ideas introduced here: that a return must be computed consistently before it can be compared, and that no return can be judged without the risk that was run to get it.
Figure F601-01 is your map.
Figure F601-01. Chapter 1 roadmap: how a return is measured, and the risks behind it.
