1.4  The four risks a treasurer names
The outcome names four risks specifically, and each of them can be pointed at in Orontes's own statements.
Credit risk is the risk that somebody who owes money does not pay. Orontes carries $4,144,000 of receivables net of an allowance of $156,000, which is the company's own estimate of the credit risk it is running on its customers. A lender carries the same risk the other way round, which is why Chapter 9 of this book deals with ratings.
Foreign exchange risk is the risk that a rate moves against a position. Orontes imports sesame, so a fall in the dollar raises its input cost and squeezes the gross margin that Book 1 spent a chapter on. There are three kinds, and the exam separates them: transaction exposure on a contract already struck, translation exposure on the statements of a foreign subsidiary, and economic exposure on the long-run competitiveness of the business.
Interest rate risk is the risk that a change in rates changes the value of an instrument or the cost of a borrowing. Orontes has $6,000,000 of long-term debt and $400,000 of it due within the year, so a rate rise reaches it at refinancing rather than immediately. A bondholder meets the same risk as a fall in price, which Chapter 4 measures with duration.
Market risk, in the narrow sense used here, is the risk that the price of a traded instrument moves. Orontes holds $42,000 of trading securities and $88,500 of debt securities, and the $4,000 of unrealised gains in its income statement is market risk showing up in reported profit.
Figure F601-05 collects them.
Figure F601-05. Four risks, and where each one touches Orontes
@table
Risk | What it is | Orontes's exposure | Managed by
Credit risk | A counterparty does not pay | Receivables of 4,144,000 | Credit policy, allowance, factoring
Foreign exchange risk | A rate moves against a position | Imported sesame; any foreign sale | Forwards, matching, pricing
Interest rate risk | Rates change value or cost | 6,000,000 of long-term debt | Fixed rates, swaps, maturity choice
Market risk | A traded price moves | 42,000 of trading securities | Position size, maturity, quality
@end
